    difficulty: 3,
    description: 'A short psych-up routine of sharp, forceful breaths used before a maximal lift or sprint to raise alertness. It is brief on purpose and differs from bracing for the lift itself.',
    instructions: ['Stand near the bar and take 5 to 10 quick, strong breaths: sharp inhale by nose, forceful exhale by mouth.', 'Finish with one normal breath, then set up and brace as you usually do for the lift.', 'Limit it to a few seconds; prolonged fast breathing causes dizziness and tingling and weakens performance.', 'Stop if you feel light-headed, and never do it under a loaded bar, in water or while driving.', 'Avoid it if you have heart disease, high blood pressure or a history of fainting.'],
